/*
    On sets, `+` is ADDITIVE union: the result retains every contribution from both
    operands, so `#(A + B) = #A + #B` always holds.
    Where the operands overlap the result is therefore a MULTISET:
    `{1, 2} + {2, 3}` denotes `{* 1, 2, 2, 3 *}`.
    This is not `|`. `|` unifies common members and is idempotent; `+` keeps them all and
    is not. The relation between the two mirrors the one between the set definition
    `{ ... }` and the multiset definition `{* ... *}`.
*/

{ 1, 2 } + { 2, 3 }
